---
metadata:
  name: quality-tree-panel
  description: One judge-jev quality tree as its checks and every path through it. Variables come from scripts/tree_vars.py.
required_variables:
  - tree
  - calls
  - columns
  - paths
  - counts
---
<section class="jj-panel jj-tree" id="tree-{{ tree.kind }}" data-tree="{{ tree.id }}" data-sha256="{{ tree.sha256 }}">
  <header class="jj-head">
    <p class="jj-eyebrow jj-mono">{{ tree.id }} · tree for {{ tree.kind_label }} records · version {{ tree.version }}</p>
    <h2>Every {{ tree.kind_label }} {{ tree.unit }} faces these checks, in this order.</h2>
    <p class="jj-lede">The first check that fails ends it and the record's verdict is no. Left: the check and where each answer leads. Right: the exact words Jev is sent.</p>
    <p class="jj-legend"><span class="jj-chip jj-ok">answer continues</span><span class="jj-chip jj-bad">answer stops: verdict no</span><span class="jj-chip jj-nx">answer asks another question</span><span class="jj-chip jj-dg">asked, never decides</span></p>
  </header>
{% for call in calls %}
  <p class="jj-eyebrow">Call {{ call.n }} · {{ call.asked_of }}{% if call.only_after %} · only after an answer of {{ call.only_after }}{% endif %}</p>
{% for check in call.checks %}
  <div class="jj-check" data-node="{{ call.node }}" data-question="{{ check.id }}">
    <div class="jj-q">
      <p class="jj-eyebrow jj-mono">{{ check.n }} · {{ check.id }}</p>
      <h3>{{ check.label }}</h3>
      <p class="jj-chips">{% for c in check.choices %}<span class="jj-chip jj-{{ c.outcome }}" data-choice="{{ c.name }}" data-leads="{{ c.leads }}" data-rule="{{ c.rule }}">{{ c.name }} → {{ c.leads }}</span>{% endfor %}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="jj-asked">
      <p class="jj-eyebrow">Jev is asked</p>
      <p class="jj-question">{{ check.asked }}</p>
{% for c in check.choices %}
      <p><b>{{ c.name }}</b> · {{ c.meaning }}</p>
{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
{% if call.diagnostics %}
  <div class="jj-check jj-dashed">
    <div class="jj-q">
      <p class="jj-eyebrow">Also asked in call {{ call.n }}</p>
      <h3>{{ call.diagnostics | length }} question{% if call.diagnostics | length > 1 %}s{% endif %} that never decide{% if call.diagnostics | length == 1 %}s{% endif %}</h3>
      <p class="jj-chips">{% for d in call.diagnostics %}<span class="jj-chip jj-dg jj-mono">{{ d.id }}</span>{% endfor %}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="jj-asked">
{% for d in call.diagnostics %}
      <p><b class="jj-mono">{{ d.id }}</b> · {{ d.asked }}</p>
{% endfor %}
      <p>Their answers appear in the run report and never change the verdict.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
  <div class="jj-sub">
    <h3>The same tree as every path a {{ tree.unit }} can take</h3>
    <p class="jj-lede">{{ counts.paths }} lines, read left to right. {{ counts.yes }} end in yes. The first red answer ends a line.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="jj-scroll">
    <div class="jj-paths" style="--cols: {{ counts.columns }}">
      <div class="jj-path jj-eyebrow"><div>Path</div>{% for col in columns %}<div>{{ col.n }} · {{ col.label }}</div>{% endfor %}<div>Ends in</div></div>
{% for p in paths %}
      <div class="jj-path" data-path="{{ p.n }}" data-verdict="{{ p.verdict }}"><div class="jj-mono jj-n">{{ p.n }}</div>{% for c in p.cells %}<div class="jj-cell jj-{{ c.k }}" data-question="{{ c.q }}" data-choices="{{ c.choices | join('|') }}">{{ c.t }}</div>{% endfor %}<div class="jj-cell jj-{% if p.verdict == 'yes' %}ok{% else %}bad{% endif %}">Verdict: {{ p.verdict }}{% if p.stop %} · {{ p.stop }}{% endif %}</div></div>
{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="jj-notes">
    <p><b>Not used</b> means the question was asked in the same call, but an earlier red answer already ended the line.</p>
{% if calls | length > 1 %}
    <p><b>Not asked</b> means no later call was made.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if tree.per == 'statement' %}
    <p><b>A record</b> gets verdict no when any one of its statements ends in no.</p>
{% endif %}
    <p><b>A verdict of yes is not yet a pass.</b> The gate also needs every deciding answer to score 0.60 or more.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="jj-foot jj-mono">source: {{ tree.source }} · sha256 {{ tree.sha256 }}</p>
</section>
